   "success": true,
   "error": null,
   "response_text": "Fixed and verified. \ud83d\udc36\n\n**Cause:** In `invkit/pricing.py`, `bulk_discount()` gated the discount with `if quantity > BULK_THRESHOLD:` \u2014 a strict comparison. Since `BULK_THRESHOLD = 10`, exactly 10 units fell through to `return 0.0`, while 11+ got the 5% off. Off-by-one, classic boundary bug.\n\n**Fix:** One-character change to inclusive comparison:\n\n```python\nif quantity >= BULK_THRESHOLD:\n    return round(quantity * unit_price * BULK_RATE, 2)\nreturn 0.0\n```\n\n**Verification:**\n- 10 units \u2192 discount `3.75` (5% of 75.00) \u2705\n- 9 units \u2192 `0.0` (still excluded) \u2705\n- 11 units \u2192 `4.12` (unchanged behavior) \u2705\n- Existing test suite: `4 passed`, no test files touched \u2014 only `invkit/pricing.py`.\n\nNo test files were added, edited, or deleted; the change is confined to library source.\n\nDONE",
